WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:05.750
Iceland.

00:00:06.791 --> 00:00:08.458
A place of waterfalls,

00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:10.958
glaciers,

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.750
hot springs,

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:18.125
and endless roads through some of 
the most dramatic landscapes on earth.

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:24.208
My name is Allan, and after several trips to Iceland,

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:27.083
it has become one of my favorite countries to visit,

00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:31.333
this itinerary is based on 
my own experiences in Iceland.

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:35.833
Over the next 7 days, I'll cover some 
of Iceland’s most essential spots

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.291
but also go beyond the typical tourist route 
to explore lesser-known places,

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:41.958
So if that sounds good to you,

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:44.291
and you’re up for an adventure in Iceland.

00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:48.333
Then this is how I would spend 7 days in Iceland.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.666
Our route focuses on the southern part of Iceland 
along with some detours into the highlands.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.041
We start with some highlights 
of the famous Golden Circle,

00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:06.166
before heading into the remote Highlands 
for some incredible scenery.

00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:11.291
We then follow along the southern coast, stopping at waterfalls

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:13.500
canyons,

00:01:13.791 --> 00:01:15.666
and glaciers along the way.

00:01:18.041 --> 00:01:21.833
This itinerary is best done between July to early September.

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:26.875
This is when most of Iceland is open, 
including the Highlands that we’ll be visiting.

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:32.958
For that, you’ll need a 4x4, 
to drive on Iceland’s famous F-roads,

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:37.458
these are rugged unpaved mountain roads 
that are only open during the summer season.

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:39.666
You don’t need the biggest vehicle 
to follow this route.

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:41.583
Something like a Suzuki Jimny,

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:44.250
or a Dacia Duster

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.916
will be enough for the roads ahead.

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:54.458
I personally went with a 4x4 camper van. 
It was my kitchen, home, and wheels all in one.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.575
Being able to cook simple meals 
and camp whenever I wanted,

00:01:58.575 --> 00:02:00.848
gave me the ultimate sense of freedom.

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:06.958
But most importantly, it was capable enough 
to handle the rugged F-roads on my journey.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.250
If you want to rent a car in Iceland, 
then check out Northbound.

00:02:10.541 --> 00:02:14.833
It’s a car rental platform that compares 
car rental companies in Iceland.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:19.958
I’ve used Northbound in the past and it’s great to be able to compare prices to get the best deal possible.

00:02:19.958 --> 00:02:24.250
You can rent anything from a regular car 
to a large 4x4 like a Landcruiser,

00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:27.791
or you can even rent the camper van 
that I had on this trip.

